+# Design analysis for the D17 variant
+# ----------------------------------
+# a) Concrete behavior / trace
+#    - Input still contains one teal(8) plus-sign cross with a center hole on a black background.
+#    - New element: several isolated red(2) single-pixel obstacles are added away from the cross.
+#    - Output keeps those red pixels unchanged. The four teal spirals are generated by the same
+#      right-turn-first turtle logic as the base task, but red cells count as solid blockers.
+#    - Small trace: if a turtle wants to continue straight for length 2 and the next cell is a red
+#      obstacle, the original task would have painted through that cell because it was black. In the
+#      variant, `can_move` rejects that straight option, so the turtle tries right-turn first,
+#      otherwise straight partial-1, otherwise left (if not on border), otherwise stops. The visual
+#      difference is not just a preserved red dot: the nearby teal corridor bends or truncates.
+# b) Complexity calibration
+#    - Obstacles are limited to one fixed visible color and to isolated single pixels. This keeps the
+#      new rule readable from 2-4 examples while still producing nontrivial rerouting.
+#    - We require 2-4 obstacles per generated instance and force them onto cells that belong to the
+#      obstacle-free spiral, so the variant does not collapse back to the base task.
+# c) Hidden assumptions in the original solver
